  <body>
    <div id="root"><div role="region" aria-label="Notifications (F8)" tabindex="-1" style="pointer-events: none;"><ol tabindex="-1" class="fixed top-0 z-[100] flex max-h-screen w-full flex-col-reverse p-4 sm:bottom-0 sm:right-0 sm:top-auto sm:flex-col md:max-w-[420px]"></ol></div><div class="min-h-screen flex flex-col"><nav class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 transition-all duration-300 bg-cream/80 backdrop-blur-md"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8"><div class="flex items-center justify-between h-[4.5rem]"><a class="flex items-center gap-2.5 group" aria-label="SPACE — home" href="/"><span class="text-ink transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-60"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 18 18" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true" class="flex-shrink-0"><rect x="0" y="0" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.9"></rect><rect x="7" y="0" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"></rect><rect x="13" y="0" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.25"></rect><rect x="0" y="7" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"></rect><rect x="7" y="7" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.9"></rect><rect x="13" y="7" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"></rect><rect x="0" y="13" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.25"></rect><rect x="7" y="13" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.5"></rect><rect x="13" y="13" width="5" height="5" rx="1" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.9"></rect></svg></span><span class="text-ink font-display font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] text-[1.0625rem] transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-60">SPACE</span></a><div class="hidden md:flex items-center gap-8"><a class="type-ui transition-colors duration-200 font-normal text-ink-muted hover:text-ink" href="/how-it-works/">How It Works</a><a class="type-ui transition-colors duration-200 font-normal text-ink-muted hover:text-ink" href="/sell/">Sell</a><a class="type-ui transition-colors duration-200 font-normal text-ink-muted hover:text-ink" href="/calculator/">Calculator</a><a class="type-ui px-5 py-2 rounded-full bg-brand text-white hover:bg-brand-hover transition-colors duration-200" href="/apply/">Request a free catalog review</a></div><button class="md:hidden p-2 -mr-1 text-ink-muted hover:text-ink transition-colors" aria-label="Open menu"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-menu h-[18px] w-[18px]"><line x1="4" x2="20" y1="12" y2="12"></line><line x1="4" x2="20" y1="6" y2="6"></line><line x1="4" x2="20" y1="18" y2="18"></line></svg></button></div></div><div class="md:hidden overflow-hidden transition-all duration-300 ease-out max-h-0 opacity-0"><div class="border-t border-black/[0.08] bg-cream/98 backdrop-blur-2xl px-6 py-5"><div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5"><a class="type-ui py-3.5 transition-colors font-normal text-ink-muted hover:text-ink" href="/how-it-works/">How It Works</a><a class="type-ui py-3.5 transition-colors font-normal text-ink-muted hover:text-ink" href="/sell/">Sell</a><a class="type-ui py-3.5 transition-colors font-normal text-ink-muted hover:text-ink" href="/calculator/">Calculator</a><div class="pt-4 mt-3 border-t border-black/[0.08] space-y-2"><a class="type-ui block text-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-full bg-brand text-white hover:bg-brand-hover transition-colors" href="/apply/">Request a free catalog review</a></div></div></div></div></nav><main class="flex-grow pt-28 pb-20 md:pt-36 md:pb-28"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4"><nav class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-8"><a class="hover:underline" href="/guides/best-music-rights-buyers-2026/">Guides</a><span class="mx-2">/</span><span>Valuation Guide</span></nav><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-4">By SPACE. Reviewed September 7, 2026. Educational guide; not an independent appraisal.</p><h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[1.15] mb-8">Music Catalog Valuation Guide 2026: How Much Is Your Catalog Worth?</h1><div class="bg-white border border-black/10 rounded-xl p-5 mb-10"><p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-wider mb-2">TL;DR</p><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">A music catalog's value depends on the future net income a buyer expects from the specific rights being acquired, and the uncertainty around that income. Annual net income multiplied by an assumed multiple can illustrate a sale scenario, but it is not a verified market price or a guaranteed offer. Documented earnings and transferable rights are the starting point for an individual review.</p></div><p class="text-lg text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed mb-14">Start with what is being sold, not a headline deal price. Ten recordings, a publisher's share of compositions, and a limited share of royalty income are different assets. This guide explains a transparent calculation, the evidence a buyer may examine and how to prepare for review. It does not present unsupported genre multiples, a proprietary benchmark or a claim about SPACE's acquisition volume. Educational information only, not an independent appraisal or legal or tax advice.</p><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">How Music Catalogs Are Valued</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">First define the tracks, rights, territory, ownership share and term. Then establish the net income attributable to that scope. Review consistent reporting periods, not just a recent viral month. Gross revenue, distributor receipts and the amount available after contractual payouts and costs are not interchangeable. If a statement has already deducted a cost, do not deduct it again.<br><br>A simple scenario uses annual net income multiplied by an assumed multiple. A more detailed income approach models expected future cash flows and discounts them to present value; a market approach compares genuinely similar transactions. These methods depend on assumptions and need not produce the same result. <a href="https://www.wipo.int/en/web/business/ip-valuation">WIPO's explanation of IP valuation methods</a> supports this distinction, not a music-specific price table. Net publisher share is a publishing-specific income measure; it should not be treated as a universal label for all master and publishing receipts.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">A Hypothetical Catalog Valuation Example</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Assume that the defined rights produce $1,000 in monthly net income. Annualizing gives $12,000. If you choose an illustrative 4x annual-income multiple and sell 50% of those rights, the scenario is $1,000 x 12 x 4 x 50% = $24,000.<br><br>The 4x input is arbitrary for this example. It is not a recommended multiple, a market benchmark or a SPACE offer. There is no additional multiplication by years, and no predicted plus-or-minus price band. If the $1,000 already describes only your owned share, the 50% refers to half of that share. Taxes, transaction deductions, outstanding balances and payment conditions are separate from this arithmetic.<br><br><a href="/calculator/">Build your own catalog sale scenario</a>, or <a href="/apply/">request a free individual catalog review</a>.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">Revenue Multiple Ranges by Genre</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">There is no verified, generally applicable 2026 multiple table on this page. A published transaction price is not enough to calculate a comparable multiple unless the income period, net-income definition, acquired rights, share, term and payment structure are also known. A major artist's catalog deal is not automatically comparable to an independent catalog.<br><br>Genre can help describe how music is used, but it does not establish a price. Ambient, mood, meditation, wellness, lo-fi, nature soundscapes, pop, rock, hip-hop, R&amp;B, country, classical and jazz catalogs all require their own evidence. Use the genre table below as a set of review questions, not as a ranking of expected returns.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">Key Factors That Affect Valuation</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Review revenue consistency, growth or decline, catalog age, track concentration, platform mix, contracts, rights clarity and the costs required to maintain earnings. A catalog dependent on one track, playlist or license has a different risk profile from one with several durable sources. Diversification may reduce concentration, but it does not guarantee a higher price.<br><br>Treat proposed sync placements, wellness-app licensing, gaming uses and short-form-video exposure as potential opportunities unless supported by agreements and receipts. Separate existing income from a buyer's growth assumptions. Metadata quality helps the reviewer match the assets and payments; it does not by itself prove ownership or justify a particular premium.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">The Role of Streaming Data</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Royalty statements establish earnings; audience dashboards help explain them. Reconcile income by platform, track, territory and reporting period before interpreting listener retention, saves, playlist sources or promotional activity. A stream count alone cannot establish the net income available to the rights owner.<br><br><a href="https://loudandclear.byspotify.com/faqs/how-do-artists-and-songwriters-get-paid/">Spotify explains that it pays rights holders</a>, whose agreements determine payments to artists and songwriters. There is no single fixed per-stream payment that reliably converts every catalog's streams into sale value. Document release spikes, one-off campaigns and unusual adjustments. A playlist placement or viral moment does not guarantee durable revenue or a higher acquisition multiple.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">Rights Clarity and Its Impact on Value</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Identify recording rights separately from composition and publishing rights. Confirm what you own, what you administer, which shares belong to collaborators and which permissions are required for a transfer. Distribution agreements, licenses, advances, sample permissions and earlier assignments can affect what is available to sell.<br><br>For US copyright ownership transfers, the written-signature requirement and rules on partial transfers are set out in <a href="https://www.copyright.gov/title17/92chap2.html">17 USC Chapter 2</a>. Other jurisdictions and particular contracts require their own legal review. Unresolved rights can delay or prevent a transaction; this guide does not assign an unsupported percentage discount. Registration and a complete spreadsheet are useful records, not guarantees that every legal risk is resolved.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">Documents to Prepare for a Catalog Review</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Prepare a track list with recording identifiers, work identifiers where available, release dates and rights ownership shares. Gather original royalty statements with reporting periods, currencies, fees, adjustments and payouts. Keep a reconciliation showing how those statements support the net-income figure you use.<br><br>Collect executed distribution, publishing, producer, co-writer, sample, licensing and earlier acquisition agreements that affect the proposed sale. List advances, unrecouped balances, liens, disputes, transfer restrictions and licenses that continue after closing. Mark unknowns as unresolved instead of guessing. A useful initial package includes the available recent history, with older statements retained to explain trends; the reviewer will confirm which periods and additional documents are needed. Do not post private statements or login credentials publicly.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">How to Increase Your Catalog's Value Before Selling</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Make the existing evidence easier to verify first. Reconcile royalty records, correct inaccurate credits and resolve conflicting ownership information. <a href="https://isrc.ifpi.org/why-use-isrc/ownership">IFPI states that ISRC identifies a recording, not its ownership</a>. <a href="https://www.iswc.org/iswc">ISWC identifies a musical work, not its ownership shares</a>. Keep identifiers linked to the actual contracts and statements.<br><br>Review registrations and collection arrangements with the appropriate organizations for your rights and territories. Consider distribution, legitimate promotion, companion content, remasters, compilations, sync or direct licensing only where the costs, permissions and commercial case make sense. A new recording or release strategy can change costs and rights scope. Do not spend on playlist placement or new releases solely because you expect a promised valuation uplift; none is established here.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">The Valuation Process at SPACE</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">SPACE is a direct buyer, not an independent adviser acting for the seller. Start with the existing application and provide the requested evidence privately during review. SPACE considers revenue history, consistency, platform mix, rights, metadata, track concentration and licensing utility. Using the calculator does not submit an application or generate an offer.<br><br>The <a href="/pricing.md">SPACE pricing and offer policy</a> provides for a free application and initial review, no listing fee or auction commission, and no obligation to accept. If the catalog is a fit, an initial offer typically follows within 5-7 business days after the relevant information is received. Payment is by bank transfer after the agreement is complete and rights-transfer requirements are satisfied. No universal closing date, guaranteed multiple, automatic eligibility threshold or acquisition-count claim is made here.</p></section><section class="mb-14"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-4">Practical Seller Checklists</h2><p class="text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed"><a href="/blog/music-catalog-sale-documents-checklist/">Music Catalog Sale Documents: A Seller's Checklist</a><br><br><a href="/blog/music-catalog-offer-checklist/">Music Catalog Offer Checklist: Questions Before You Sign</a></p></section><section class="mb-20"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Genre Evidence to Review</h2><div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse"><thead><tr class="border-b border-black/10"><th class="text-left py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Genre</th><th class="text-left py-3 px-4 font-medium">Pricing basis</th><th class="text-left py-3 pl-4 font-medium">Key Factors</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Pop and Rock</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Separate recurring catalog income from release campaigns and one-off licenses; verify the acquired rights and historical periods.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Hip-Hop and R&amp;B</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Confirm producer and collaborator interests, sample permissions, contracts and the durability of reported earnings.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Country</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Distinguish recording and publishing income and reconcile streaming, radio-related and licensing receipts where relevant.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Ambient and Mood</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Check track and playlist concentration, platform dependence and recurring income rather than assuming utility listening implies a premium.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Lo-Fi and Beats</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Check beat-license terms, exclusivity, collaborator shares and the specific recordings or income interests offered.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Meditation and Wellness</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Distinguish executed app or service licenses from prospective licensing opportunities and confirm renewal and assignment terms.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Nature Soundscapes</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Document source recordings, permissions and the rights claimed; review licensing scope and income concentration.</td></tr><tr class="border-b border-black/[0.06]"><td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium">Classical and Jazz</td><td class="py-3 px-4 text-foreground font-medium">Individual review</td><td class="py-3 pl-4 text-muted-foreground">Separate rights in recordings, arrangements and compositions; confirm which income and permissions the seller actually controls.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="mb-20"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Valuation Factors at a Glance</h2><div class="grid gap-4"><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-red-700">High impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Revenue Consistency</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Use comparable periods and explain seasonality, reporting delays and unusual adjustments. Stability is evidence to evaluate, not a guaranteed premium.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-red-700">High impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Revenue Growth Trend</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Separate recurring growth from one-off spikes and record the costs required to sustain it.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700">Medium impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Platform Diversity</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Document income by source to identify dependence on a single service, playlist, license or track.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700">Medium impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Playlist Inclusion</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Describe the source and duration of listening. Placement is not a promise of continued exposure or earnings.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-red-100 text-red-700">High impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Rights Clarity</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Match claimed ownership to agreements and disclose unresolved permissions, disputes or encumbrances. Issues may need resolution before an offer.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700">Medium impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Genre Demand</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Explain evidenced use cases and licensing activity. Genre alone does not establish a multiple.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700">Medium impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Catalog Age</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Older records may help assess durability. A longer history does not automatically establish future performance.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700">Medium impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Sync Licensing Potential</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Distinguish executed deals and collected income from possible future placements; verify who can authorize both sides of a use.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-amber-100 text-amber-700">Medium impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Metadata Quality</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Link each statement to the correct recording and work. Identifiers and credits do not replace proof of ownership.</p></div></div><div class="border border-black/10 rounded-lg p-4 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start gap-3 bg-white"><div class="flex-shrink-0"><span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-gray-100 text-gray-600">Low-Medium impact</span></div><div><p class="font-medium mb-1">Listener Demographics</p><p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">Use territory and audience information to explain observed income; do not substitute a generic per-stream rate for actual statements.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="mb-20"><h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2><div class="w-full" data-orientation="vertical"><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b border-black/10"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-:r1:" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-:r0:" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between transition-all [&amp;[data-state=open]>svg]:rotate-180 text-base font-medium py-4 hover:no-underline text-left" data-radix-collection-item="">How long does a music catalog valuation take?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-:r1:" hidden="" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-:r0:" data-orientation="vertical" class="overflow-hidden text-sm transition-all data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down" style="--radix-accordion-content-height: var(--radix-collapsible-content-height); --radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width);"></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b border-black/10"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-:r3:" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-:r2:" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between transition-all [&amp;[data-state=open]>svg]:rotate-180 text-base font-medium py-4 hover:no-underline text-left" data-radix-collection-item="">What is the minimum catalog size needed to get a valuation?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-:r3:" hidden="" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-:r2:" data-orientation="vertical" class="overflow-hidden text-sm transition-all data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down" style="--radix-accordion-content-height: var(--radix-collapsible-content-height); --radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width);"></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b border-black/10"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-:r5:" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-:r4:" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between transition-all [&amp;[data-state=open]>svg]:rotate-180 text-base font-medium py-4 hover:no-underline text-left" data-radix-collection-item="">Does selling my catalog mean I lose creative control of my music?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-:r5:" hidden="" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-:r4:" data-orientation="vertical" class="overflow-hidden text-sm transition-all data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down" style="--radix-accordion-content-height: var(--radix-collapsible-content-height); --radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width);"></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b border-black/10"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-:r7:" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-:r6:" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between transition-all [&amp;[data-state=open]>svg]:rotate-180 text-base font-medium py-4 hover:no-underline text-left" data-radix-collection-item="">How are streaming royalties factored into the valuation?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-:r7:" hidden="" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-:r6:" data-orientation="vertical" class="overflow-hidden text-sm transition-all data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down" style="--radix-accordion-content-height: var(--radix-collapsible-content-height); --radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width);"></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b border-black/10"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-:r9:" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-:r8:" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between transition-all [&amp;[data-state=open]>svg]:rotate-180 text-base font-medium py-4 hover:no-underline text-left" data-radix-collection-item="">Can I sell only part of my catalog?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-:r9:" hidden="" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-:r8:" data-orientation="vertical" class="overflow-hidden text-sm transition-all data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down" style="--radix-accordion-content-height: var(--radix-collapsible-content-height); --radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width);"></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b border-black/10"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-:rb:" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-:ra:" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between transition-all [&amp;[data-state=open]>svg]:rotate-180 text-base font-medium py-4 hover:no-underline text-left" data-radix-collection-item="">What is the difference between publishing rights and master rights?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-:rb:" hidden="" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-:ra:" data-orientation="vertical" class="overflow-hidden text-sm transition-all data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down" style="--radix-accordion-content-height: var(--radix-collapsible-content-height); --radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width);"></div></div><div data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" class="border-b border-black/10"><h3 data-orientation="vertical" data-state="closed" class="flex"><button type="button" aria-controls="radix-:rd:" aria-expanded="false" data-state="closed" data-orientation="vertical" id="radix-:rc:" class="flex flex-1 items-center justify-between transition-all [&amp;[data-state=open]>svg]:rotate-180 text-base font-medium py-4 hover:no-underline text-left" data-radix-collection-item="">How do I know if my catalog is valuable enough to sell?<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></button></h3><div data-state="closed" id="radix-:rd:" hidden="" role="region" aria-labelledby="radix-:rc:" data-orientation="vertical" class="overflow-hidden text-sm transition-all data-[state=closed]:animate-accordion-up data-[state=open]:animate-accordion-down" style="--radix-accordion-content-height: var(--radix-collapsible-content-height); --radix-accordion-content-width: var(--radix-collapsible-content-width);"></div></div></div><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does a music catalog valuation take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The calculator performs an immediate hypothetical calculation, not a reviewed valuation. SPACE typically provides an initial offer within 5-7 business days after receiving the relevant information, if the catalog is a fit. Missing evidence or complex rights may require further review."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the minimum catalog size needed to get a valuation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"This guide does not impose a track-count or revenue minimum. Contactability, rights and documented income require individual review. Submitting a catalog does not guarantee an offer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does selling my catalog mean I lose creative control of my music?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Control depends on the exact rights, approvals and obligations in the agreement. Ask what transfers and what remains yours, including any provisions affecting future work. Obtain independent legal advice rather than assuming a sale preserves every approval."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are streaming royalties factored into the valuation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Use documented income for the rights being reviewed, with consistent periods and deductions. Streaming dashboards provide context but are not a substitute for royalty statements. Explain one-off spikes, platform dependence and collection delays."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I sell only part of my catalog?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A proposal can cover selected tracks or a share of defined rights, subject to ownership and agreement. In a scenario calculation, apply the sold share once to the income base for those rights. Contractual terms still require separate review."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the difference between publishing rights and master rights?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Composition and publishing rights concern the underlying musical work; master rights concern a particular sound recording. Owners and income streams may differ. The proposed sale must identify which rights and shares are included."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do I know if my catalog is valuable enough to sell?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Gather evidence of recurring income and the rights you control, then request an individual review. A hypothetical calculator result is not evidence that a buyer will make that offer. SPACE's initial catalog review is free and carries no obligation."}}]}</script></section><section class="mb-20"><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Sources</h2><ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2"><li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://www.wipo.int/en/web/business/ip-valuation" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">WIPO: Valuing Intellectual Property Assets</a></li><li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://loudandclear.byspotify.com/faqs/how-do-artists-and-songwriters-get-paid/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">Spotify: How do artists and songwriters get paid?</a></li><li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://www.copyright.gov/title17/92chap2.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">US Copyright Office: Copyright Ownership and Transfer</a></li><li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://isrc.ifpi.org/why-use-isrc/ownership" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">IFPI: ISRC and Ownership</a></li><li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://www.iswc.org/iswc" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">ISWC: What the musical-work identifier does and does not do</a></li><li class="text-sm text-muted-foreground"><a href="https://spacemusic.io/pricing.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="hover:underline">SPACE: Pricing and Offer Policy</a></li></ol></section><section class="bg-white py-12 border-t border-black/10"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4"><p class="text-xs font-medium text-ink-muted uppercase tracking-widest mb-5">Related content</p><div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2"><div><h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-3">Core pages</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/guides/how-to-sell-music-rights/">How to Sell Music Rights</a><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/guides/best-music-rights-buyers-2026/">Best Music Rights Buyers (2026)</a><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/compare/full-buyout-vs-revenue-split/">Full Buyout vs Revenue Split</a><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/guides/how-long-does-it-take-to-sell-a-music-catalog/">How Long Does It Take to Sell?</a></div></div><div><h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-3">Glossary terms</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/glossary/catalog-valuation/">Catalog Valuation</a><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/glossary/revenue-multiple/">Revenue Multiple</a><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/glossary/master-rights/">Master Rights</a></div></div><div><h3 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink mb-3">Tools</h3><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/streaming-rates/spotify-2026/">Spotify Pay Per Stream (2026)</a><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/streaming-rates/apple-music-2026/">Apple Music Pay Per Stream (2026)</a><a class="text-sm px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-cream rounded-full border border-black/10 hover:border-black/25 transition-colors" href="/calculator/">Catalog Value Calculator</a></div></div></div></div></section><div class="p-8 md:p-10 bg-dark text-white rounded-xl text-center"><p class="text-lg font-medium mb-2">Explore a scenario or request an individual review</p><p class="text-ink-muted mb-4 text-sm">The calculator is hypothetical. A catalog review is free and carries no obligation.</p><div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-3"><a class="inline-block bg-brand text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:bg-brand-hover transition-colors" href="/calculator/">Build a Sale Scenario</a><a class="inline-block border border-white/20 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-full text-sm font-medium hover:bg-white/8 transition-colors" href="/apply/">Request a Free Catalog Review</a></div></div></div